   "provider": "Dr. Michael Snow",
   "specialty": "family medicine",
   "page_count": 1,
   "pages": [
    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "Cooper-Smith Medical Group\n\nDear Colleague,\n\nI saw Rachel Thomas in consultation on July 23, 2024. Ms. Thomas presented with concerns regarding her hypertension and vitamin D deficiency.\n\n**History of Present Illness:**\nMs. Thomas is a 50-year-old female with a history of hypertension, which was first diagnosed on May 2022. She currently takes valsartan 320 mg and lisinopril 10 mg, and her blood pressure is well-controlled at the time of this visit, measured at 130/92 mmHg. Ms. Thomas also has a history of vitamin D deficiency, initially diagnosed on May 15, 2013. She has been on ergocalciferol 50000 IU, and her levels are adequately controlled.\n\n**Physical Examination:**\nMs. Thomas appeared well, in no acute distress. Her vital signs were within normal limits with a blood pressure of 130/92 mmHg, heart rate 72 bpm, respiratory rate 16 breaths per minute, and temperature 98.6°F. Weight was 155 lbs. The rest of her physical exam was unremarkable with no significant abnormalities noted in the cardiovascular, respiratory, abdominal, or neurological exams. Her extremities showed no edema, and peripheral pulses were palpable.\n\n**Family History:**\nRelevant family history includes her father who had colon cancer at the age of 46 and passed away at 58. Additionally, her father has Alzheimer’s disease, diagnosed at age 68, and is currently living.\n\n**Social History:**\nMs. Thomas reports consuming approximately one alcoholic drink per week. She denies tobacco use. \n\n**Impression:**\nMs. Thomas is being managed effectively for her hypertension with a combination of valsartan and lisinopril. Her blood pressure is within the target range, and she is compliant with her medication regimen. Her vitamin D deficiency is also well-controlled with ergocalciferol supplementation. She has no symptoms suggestive of either condition worsening and her physical exam findings are consistent with stable health.\n\n**Recommendations:**\n1. Continue valsartan 320 mg and lisinopril 10 mg for hypertension management.\n2. Continue ergocalciferol 50000 IU for vitamin D deficiency.\n3. Regular monitoring of blood pressure and vitamin D levels is advised.\n4. Encourage maintaining her current lifestyle with minimal alcohol consumption and no tobacco use.\n\nI hope this summary is helpful. Should you have any questions or require further information, please do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Michael Snow\nFamily Medicine Specialist\nCooper-Smith Medical Group\n"
    }
